      "slug": "peeling-black-eyed-beans",
      "term": "Peeling black-eyed beans",
      "definition": "Soaking dried black-eyed beans, then rubbing them between your palms to remove the skins. Skinless beans blend to a smoother, lighter batter."
    },
    {
      "slug": "steaming-moulds",
      "term": "Steaming moulds",
      "definition": "Containers used to hold the batter while it steams. Traditionally banana leaves or small aluminium cans. Small ramekins or heatproof cups work well at home."
    }
  ],
