  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key preparation step is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "peeling black-eyed beans ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "peeling-black-eyed-beans"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Skin-on beans make a grainy batter. Once the skins are off, the beans blend to a very smooth paste. Pour the batter into "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "steaming moulds",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "steaming-moulds"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and steam until firm to the touch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The batter should pour like a thick smoothie. If it is stiffer than that, add a little more water before steaming."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-eyed-beans",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "dried, soaked overnight, skins rubbed off and discarded",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "pepper-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "roughly chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "onion",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "roughly chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "deseeded if preferred",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sunflower-oil",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "or palm oil if available",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "beaten",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": "or to taste",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend peeled black-eyed beans with the red pepper, onion and chilli, adding 150ml water. Blend until completely smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer to a bowl. Stir in the oil, eggs (if using) and salt. The batter should flow like thick cream."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grease small heatproof cups or ramekins with oil. Fill each about two-thirds full with batter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Set a steamer over simmering water. Steam cups for 40 to 45 minutes until firm to the touch and a skewer comes out clean."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Allow to cool for 5 minutes before turning out. Serve warm or at room temperature."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Moin moin is grainy",
              "cause": "Skins not fully removed or not blended long enough",
              "fix": "Rub soaked beans vigorously between your palms until the skins float off. Blend for at least 2 minutes until the paste is silky."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Moin moin did not set",
              "cause": "Batter too thin or understeamed",
              "fix": "The batter must be thick enough to hold its shape when poured. Steam for at least 40 minutes and check with a skewer."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Moin moin is central to Yoruba food culture and sold everywhere from street stalls to home kitchens. It appears at naming ceremonies, weddings and Sunday breakfasts alongside akara and ogi (corn porridge). The dish is sometimes enriched with crayfish, smoked fish or diced boiled eggs folded into the batter before steaming."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}